  "source": "icanspeak Italian original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-12)",
  "subtitle": "In Italian, the thing you like is the subject: mi piace il caffè (coffee pleases me). One thing or an action: mi piace. More than one thing: mi piacciono.",
  "briefMarks": ["mi piace", "mi piacciono", "anche a me", "neanche a me"],
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "(a me)" },
      { "text": "mi / ti / gli / le / ci / vi", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "piace / piacciono", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "what you like" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-prep\">Mi</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">piace</span> il caffè. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Mi</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">piacciono</span> i cani. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Non mi</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">piace</span> cucinare. · <span class=\"vp-prep\">Ti</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">piace</span> Torino?",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>piace</strong> with one thing or a verb: <em>Mi piace la musica. Mi piace ballare.</em> <strong>piacciono</strong> with more than one thing: <em>Mi piacciono i cani.</em>",
        "tag": "piace or piacciono"
      },
      {
        "html": "The small word shows <strong>who likes it</strong>: <em>mi</em> (I), <em>ti</em> (you), <em>gli</em> (he), <em>le</em> (she), <em>Le</em> (you, polite), <em>ci</em> (we), <em>vi</em> (you all), <em>gli</em> (they).",
        "tag": "Who likes it"
      },
      {
        "html": "Use the article with the noun: <em>Mi piace <strong>il</strong> calcio.</em> Not: <em>Mi piace calcio.</em> No article with a verb: <em>Mi piace leggere.</em>",
        "tag": "Use the article"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>non</strong> goes first: <em>Non mi piace il pesce.</em> To name the person, use <strong>a</strong> and no small word: <em>A Luca piace correre. Ai miei figli piace il parco.</em>",
        "tag": "non, a"
      },
      {
        "html": "To agree, say <strong>anche a me</strong> (me too) after a positive and <strong>neanche a me</strong> (me neither) after a negative. To disagree: <em>A me no. / A me sì.</em>",
        "tag": "Me too"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Io piaccio il caffè</em> → ✓ <em>Mi piace il caffè</em>. ✗ <em>Mi piace i cani</em> → ✓ <em>Mi piacciono i cani</em>. ✗ <em>A Luca gli piace</em> in writing → ✓ <em>A Luca piace</em> or <em>Gli piace</em> (you will hear <em>a me mi piace</em> in speech, but don't write it). ✗ <em>Anche a me</em> after a negative → ✓ <em>Neanche a me</em>. A polite wish uses <em>vorrei</em>: <em>Vorrei un caffè, per favore.</em> Next: <a href=\"/indirect-object-pronouns\">Indirect object pronouns</a>.",
